{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"9996224c-2106-44c1-a174-77c6b81ca60f","runId":"1d590b89-383d-442f-90d6-a93aa0a146e7","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":9,"previousEventHash":"sha256:61e5aae5e7815149e49dcf0ac37ef23327487c17c2fc8e77078d035e5bcc1aad","type":"node.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a039fc-a8fa-798e-be67-c2073dbf37fd","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-25T18:04:38.246Z","idempotencyKey":"node:investigate-1:completed","payload":{"nodeId":"investigate-1","node":"investigate","attempt":1,"round":1,"headSha":"03e6133becc50ba8509b976743ea76ffeaab2c4d","baseSha":"03e6133becc50ba8509b976743ea76ffeaab2c4d","outcome":"confirmed","verificationResults":[],"evidence":["`src/core/dispatcher.ts` derives the ordinary next-node `headSha` only from completed `prepare-pr` or `verify` records; when `verify-1` is selected immediately after `implement-1`, neither exists, so the implementation head is omitted.","The remediation path in `src/core/dispatcher.ts` supplies new round nodes with the latest `prepare-pr` head, which can bind `verify-2` to the prior round rather than the newly completed `implement-2` head.","`src/workflows/work-on.ts` records only `baseSha` in initial bounded-node queued, launch-intent started, and receipt-bound resumed payloads; it does not project `node.headSha` into those events or their durable snapshot.","`src/workflows/work-on.ts` forwards `reviewHeadSha` only for reviewer nodes. Although its launch input carries the node object, verify has no equivalent trusted head binding or dispatch-time clean-worktree/head assertion.","`src/adapters/subagents.ts` includes only the frozen base SHA in bounded task text. Approved check names are rendered only by the legacy unbounded work-on prompt; the bounded verify prompt receives no command-name list.","`src/adapters/subagents.ts` does place the validated policy's full `verificationCommands` map in the protected extension binding, and `src/agents/child-runtime.ts` makes `forge_verify` reject unknown names, but the read-only model has no supported way to enumerate that opaque map.","Existing tests cover frozen reviewer heads and the generic bounded investigate prompt, but do not assert implementation-head or approved-check-name handoff for bounded verify nodes."]}}
